<title>ISRAEL: Israel's financial markets closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Israel's financial markets closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's stock and bond markets are closed on Sunday for the Jewish holiday of Purim. The Tel Aviv bourse will reopen on Monday.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
